cli (wasm): homescoop's allocator refresh as the global allocator (homescoop#1287)

V8 checks a thread's memory.fill/memory.copy against that thread's cached
memory length, which can lag a memory.grow another thread's malloc just
did, so a memset into a fresh block traps "memory access out of bounds"
(slicc-kernel#1172). On wasm the binary includes
scripts/rust-wasm-refresh-alloc.rs (path in HOMESCOOP_WASM_ALLOC_RS, set by
build.sh).

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: V8 refreshes other threads' memory length before a grown block
can reach them, or the wasi-libc malloc Rust links does.

--- a/crates/cli/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/cli/src/main.rs
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@
 #[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]
 mod font_render;
 
+// homescoop#1287: threaded wasm takes homescoop's allocator refresh
+// (scripts/rust-wasm-refresh-alloc.rs) against V8's stale per-thread memory
+// length after another thread's memory.grow.
+#[cfg(target_family = "wasm")]
+include!(env!("HOMESCOOP_WASM_ALLOC_RS"));
+
 pub const VERSION: &str = env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION");
 
 #[cfg(target_family = "wasm")]
